                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "822203d2-f799-4dfa-9557-7374a93fee38",
                        "source_entry_id": "05c09311-8d60-3a90-bae8-1b689d5d3645",
                        "source_sense_id": "a594c23d-f1ac-34a2-bca3-c91bd4a87135",
                        "target_lang_word": "assassinator",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "assassinator",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "60d7d827-fc38-3ff1-97c1-60b0d9b4f5a5",
                                        "entry_id": "e6f97ae0-4b3b-3b6c-ade0-5a23f84631ab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An assassin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8646a850-b4d4-41f8-85a2-8a579104b8ff",
                                                "sense_id": "60d7d827-fc38-3ff1-97c1-60b0d9b4f5a5",
                                                "text": "Philip of Spain had offered a reward of 25,000 crowns, a patent of nobility, and immunity for all past crimes, to the assassinator of the Prince of Orange."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4a857ec6-bd53-4de9-8dc2-68ba0d020873",
                        "source_entry_id": "05c09311-8d60-3a90-bae8-1b689d5d3645",
                        "source_sense_id": "a594c23d-f1ac-34a2-bca3-c91bd4a87135",
                        "target_lang_word": "assassin",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "assassin",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "abded5cc-62c9-3310-b1fc-7e575d536e90",
                                        "entry_id": "75d527d1-d1c7-3d6e-b425-2be8c291fc70",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A member of the Nizari Ismaili Muslim community of the Alamut Period."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "capitalized",
                                            "historical",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "332d0a17-bed7-4d1a-8af7-1aa3788b4663",
                                                "sense_id": "abded5cc-62c9-3310-b1fc-7e575d536e90",
                                                "text": "The Assassines, a nation depending of Phœnicia, are esteemed among the Mahometists of a soveraigne devotion and puritie of maners; they hold, that the readiest and shortest way to gaine Paradise, is to kill some one of a contrary religion[…]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0eab14c8-4221-37e4-bda6-39fa5f3a5fec",
                                        "entry_id": "75d527d1-d1c7-3d6e-b425-2be8c291fc70",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who intentionally kills a person, especially a professional who kills a public or political figure."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b64ca3b9-118f-41cd-82b6-4d2684af6925",
                                                "sense_id": "0eab14c8-4221-37e4-bda6-39fa5f3a5fec",
                                                "text": "The hand that held the bond of so many jarring interests lay powerless beneath the pall. The perils of war had been about him, and the midnight assassin had watched his path; yet he died quietly in his bed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a13cac2-ea3d-4788-8fa0-f5508cb1e062",
                                                "sense_id": "0eab14c8-4221-37e4-bda6-39fa5f3a5fec",
                                                "text": "What has violence ever accomplished? What has it ever created? No martyr's cause can ever be stilled by an assassin’s bullet."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "07879c00-3c39-4f7f-872b-3bcb2df3246d",
                                                "sense_id": "0eab14c8-4221-37e4-bda6-39fa5f3a5fec",
                                                "text": "Even without hovering drones, a lurking assassin, a thumping score and a denouement, the real-life story of Edward Snowden, a rogue spy on the run, could be straight out of the cinema. But, as with Hollywood, the subplots and exotic locations may distract from the real message: America’s discomfort and its foes’ glee."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8a918c8f-caaf-3b21-a266-6a07e0855785",
                                        "entry_id": "75d527d1-d1c7-3d6e-b425-2be8c291fc70",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any ruthless killer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4ae7e56d-cdbf-3daf-afb1-c1f58851d737",
                                        "entry_id": "75d527d1-d1c7-3d6e-b425-2be8c291fc70",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An associated prime of a module."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "humorous"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "assassin",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "37fdc09b-cd71-3dbc-8e90-94b6670fc492",
                                        "entry_id": "f1663c8a-ad02-3ea1-a831-0f10be95ac6e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To assassinate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "nonstandard"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d2f23043-33d1-44f1-832b-8cec74b142d0",
                        "source_entry_id": "05c09311-8d60-3a90-bae8-1b689d5d3645",
                        "source_sense_id": "a594c23d-f1ac-34a2-bca3-c91bd4a87135",
                        "target_lang_word": "attacker",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "attacker",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1c85e5da-c06f-39a6-ae43-3c627ecfeb6a",
                                        "entry_id": "f7fcc3ad-74d0-3f3c-8c86-85533649bc74",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who attacks."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "596cbbf8-23bc-4a7a-bdf1-eae80f447725",
                                                "sense_id": "1c85e5da-c06f-39a6-ae43-3c627ecfeb6a",
                                                "text": "[…] expecting the woman to take her attacker into physical custody is tantamount to preventing the arrest. If she could handle him, she probably would not need to call the police in the first place."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5baaf9c5-d9c1-4440-be67-16845767a97d",
                                                "sense_id": "1c85e5da-c06f-39a6-ae43-3c627ecfeb6a",
                                                "text": "In this manner, the victim may be able to discover the one or many zombied systems that are causing the DoS attack but probably won't be able to track down the actual attacker."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6a4151d-5ed7-48be-adad-12459bd9fc72",
                                                "sense_id": "1c85e5da-c06f-39a6-ae43-3c627ecfeb6a",
                                                "text": "The targets suggest the attackers are sympathetic to the vast censorship apparatus known as the Great Firewall of China."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ecaf6c8f-2090-387a-b46d-d93b8d6ea0a7",
                                        "entry_id": "f7fcc3ad-74d0-3f3c-8c86-85533649bc74",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One of the players on a team in football (soccer) in the row nearest to the opposing team's goal, who are therefore principally responsible for scoring goals."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6351bbfe-77b0-419f-98f1-a11ef926b6be",
                        "source_entry_id": "05c09311-8d60-3a90-bae8-1b689d5d3645",
                        "source_sense_id": "a594c23d-f1ac-34a2-bca3-c91bd4a87135",
